# Day 2: 4-Bit Ripple Carry Adder

## Objective
To design and simulate a 4-bit Ripple Carry Adder using Verilog HDL.

## Tools Used
- Ubuntu Linux
- Icarus Verilog
- GTKWave

## Working Principle
A 4-bit Ripple Carry Adder consists of four Full Adders connected in series. The carry output from each Full Adder is passed to the next stage.

## Simulation
The design was compiled and simulated using Icarus Verilog. The output was checked for different binary input combinations.

## Test Results

| A | B | Cin | Cout | Sum |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0011 | 0101 | 0 | 0 | 1000 |
| 1111 | 0001 | 0 | 1 | 0000 |
| 1010 | 0101 | 1 | 1 | 0000 |

## Learning Outcome
- Understood Full Adder connections.
- Learned carry propagation.
- Practiced Verilog simulation using Icarus Verilog.
- Viewed signal waveforms using GTKWave.
